Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: run the TXQ scheduler on tx completion

A tx completion is what frees both the tx descriptor and the airtime
charged against the queue limit, so it is the moment at which the next
frames become sendable. Nothing starts a round there, so with a binding
limit the queue is only refilled when the next frame arrives from the
network stack, and the throughput collapses: on the author's IPQ8074 bench
33.7 Mbit/s without this round against 74.3 Mbit/s with it, at the same
21 ms of latency.

Start a round for the access categories that saw completions, on the radio
they completed on.

This is a backport of patch 6/9 of the series

  [PATCH ath-next v3 0/9] wifi: ath11k: airtime queue limits, fairness and
  a driver TXQ scheduler

posted to linux-wireless by Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
(message-id 20260824142350.1757379-1-julius@bairaktaris.de). The series is
not merged upstream yet and the original diffs were not reachable from the
build host, so the change was reimplemented against backports 6.18.26 from
the series description. It therefore carries no upstream Signed-off-by and
may differ from the patch that eventually lands.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
index 4cba35e..29e0bd8 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -693,9 +693,12 @@ void ath11k_dp_tx_completion_handler(struct ath11k_base *ab, int ring_id)
 	struct sk_buff *msdu;
 	struct hal_tx_status ts = {};
 	struct dp_tx_ring *tx_ring = &dp->tx_ring[ring_id];
+	u8 sched_mask[MAX_RADIOS] = {};
 	u32 *desc;
 	u32 msdu_id;
 	u8 mac_id;
+	u8 ac;
+	int i;
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&status_ring->lock);
 
@@ -759,8 +762,35 @@ void ath11k_dp_tx_completion_handler(struct ath11k_base *ab, int ring_id)
 		if (atomic_dec_and_test(&ar->dp.num_tx_pending))
 			wake_up(&ar->dp.tx_empty_waitq);
 
+		ac = skb_get_queue_mapping(msdu);
+		if (ac < IEEE80211_NUM_ACS && mac_id < MAX_RADIOS)
+			sched_mask[mac_id] |= BIT(ac);
+
 		ath11k_dp_tx_complete_msdu(ar, msdu, &ts);
 	}
+
+	/* Completions are what frees both the descriptors and the airtime
+	 * charged against the queue limit, so this is the point where the
+	 * next frames become sendable. Without a round here the queue is
+	 * only refilled when the network stack hands down the next frame,
+	 * which is what costs the throughput at a binding limit.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < MAX_RADIOS; i++) {
+		if (!sched_mask[i])
+			continue;
+
+		if (!rcu_access_pointer(ab->pdevs_active[i]))
+			continue;
+
+		ar = ab->pdevs[i].ar;
+		if (!ar)
+			continue;
+
+		for (ac = 0; ac < IEEE80211_NUM_ACS; ac++) {
+			if (sched_mask[i] & BIT(ac))
+				ath11k_mac_tx_push_pending(ar, ac);
+		}
+	}
 }
 
 int ath11k_dp_tx_send_reo_cmd(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct dp_rx_tid *rx_tid,
